# =============================================================================
# CLINE RULES CONFIGURATION - Budgeteer Project
# =============================================================================
# This file defines rules for how Cline should work with this project.
# Everything in this file (including comments) is read as instructions.
# =============================================================================

# 📚 PROJECT CONTEXT & DOCUMENTATION
# =============================================================================

# These files are automatically included in Cline's context window
@context docs/api/monzo-api.pdf
@context docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@context docs/TESTING.md
@context .cline/memory.md
@context .cline/tasks.md

# Files to read at the start of tasks to understand project state
@read .cline/memory.md
@read .cline/tasks.md
@read docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@read docs/TESTING.md

# =============================================================================
# 📁 PROJECT STRUCTURE
# =============================================================================

# This is a MONO-REPO with the following structure:
# 
# budgeteer/
# ├── backend/              # Spring Boot API
# │   ├── src/main/java/    # Java source code
# │   ├── src/main/resources/
# │   │   ├── application.properties
# │   │   └── db/migration/ # Flyway migrations
# │   └── pom.xml
# ├── frontend/             # React/Vue (future)
# ├── docs/                 # Public documentation (committed)
# │   ├── ARCHITECTURE.md
# │   ├── SETUP.md
# │   ├── MONZO-AUTH-FLOW.md
# │   └── api/monzo-api.pdf
# ├── scripts/              # Development scripts
# │   └── dev.sh
# ├── .cline/               # Cline AI context (git-ignored)
# │   ├── memory.md         # Session memory
# │   ├── tasks.md          # Task board
# │   └── notes/            # Cline working notes
# ├── .notes/               # Personal scratch work (git-ignored)
# ├── compose.yaml          # Docker services
# ├── .env                  # Local secrets (git-ignored)
# ├── README.md             # Project readme
# └── CONTRIBUTING.md       # Git conventions

# =============================================================================
# 🎯 WORKING GUIDELINES
# =============================================================================

# When working on this project, Cline should:

# PROJECT MANAGEMENT
# 1. Check .cline/memory.md for current status and context
# 2. Review .cline/tasks.md for the task board and priorities
# 3. Reference docs/ARCHITECTURE.md before making significant changes
# 4. Update .cline/memory.md with important decisions and context

# MONZO API INTEGRATION
# 5. Reference docs/api/monzo-api.pdf when implementing Monzo API integrations
# 6. Follow docs/MONZO-AUTH-FLOW.md for OAuth implementation details
# 7. Never log or expose access tokens or refresh tokens

# MONO-REPO AWARENESS
# 8. Backend code lives in backend/src/
# 9. Run Maven commands from backend/ directory
# 10. Docker compose runs from project root

# =============================================================================
# 💻 CODE STYLE & STANDARDS
# =============================================================================

# JAVA/SPRING BOOT
# - Follow Google Java Style Guide
# - Use meaningful, descriptive variable and method names
# - Add Javadoc comments for all public classes and methods
# - Use constructor injection over field injection for dependencies
# - Keep controllers thin - business logic belongs in services
# - Use DTOs for API requests/responses, not entities directly

# PACKAGE STRUCTURE (in backend/src/main/java/)
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.controller   - REST controllers
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.service      - Business logic
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.repository   - Data access
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.model        - Entities and DTOs
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.config       - Configuration classes
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.exception    - Custom exceptions
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.client       - External API clients (Monzo)

# =============================================================================
# 🧪 TESTING REQUIREMENTS
# =============================================================================

# When writing new code:
# - Write unit tests for all service methods
# - Use @WebMvcTest for controller tests
# - Use @DataJpaTest for repository tests  
# - Use @SpringBootTest sparingly (integration tests only)
# - Mock external services (Monzo API) in tests
# - Aim for meaningful test coverage, not 100% line coverage

# =============================================================================
# 🔀 GIT WORKFLOW
# =============================================================================

# See CONTRIBUTING.md for full details

# BRANCHING
# - main          - Production-ready code
# - feature/*     - New features (e.g., feature/monzo-oauth)
# - fix/*         - Bug fixes
# - refactor/*    - Code improvements
# - docs/*        - Documentation updates
# - chore/*       - Maintenance tasks

# COMMITS - Use Conventional Commits
# - feat:     New feature (feat: add transaction sync endpoint)
# - fix:      Bug fix (fix: handle null account balance)
# - docs:     Documentation (docs: update API documentation)
# - refactor: Code refactoring (refactor: extract MonzoClient)
# - test:     Test additions (test: add UserService unit tests)
# - chore:    Maintenance (chore: update dependencies)

# =============================================================================
# 📋 COMMON TASK TEMPLATES
# =============================================================================

# When asked to "add a new REST endpoint":
# 1. Create/update controller in backend/src/.../controller/
# 2. Add service layer method with business logic
# 3. Create/update repository if data access needed
# 4. Create request/response DTOs if needed
# 5. Write unit tests for service and controller
# 6. Update API documentation

# When asked to "add a new entity":
# 1. Create entity class with JPA annotations
# 2. Create repository interface
# 3. Add Flyway migration in backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/
# 4. Create DTOs for API exposure
# 5. Add to docs/ARCHITECTURE.md if significant

# When asked to "integrate with Monzo API":
# 1. Check docs/api/monzo-api.pdf for endpoint details
# 2. Check docs/MONZO-AUTH-FLOW.md for auth requirements
# 3. Add method to MonzoClient
# 4. Create appropriate DTOs
# 5. Handle rate limits and errors gracefully

# =============================================================================
# ⚡ AUTO-APPROVE COMMANDS
# =============================================================================

# These commands run without asking for approval each time.
@auto-approve cd backend && mvn clean install -DskipTests
@auto-approve cd backend && mvn spring-boot:run
@auto-approve cd backend && mvn test
@auto-approve docker compose up -d
@auto-approve docker compose down
@auto-approve ./scripts/dev.sh

# =============================================================================
# 🏁 TASK CLOSURE PROTOCOL
# =============================================================================

# When user says "close task", "close this task", or "finish task":
# Cline should automatically perform these steps:
#
# 1. UPDATE .cline/tasks.md:
#    - Move the current task from "🚀 In Progress" to "✅ Done" section
#    - Add completion date (format: January YYYY)
#    - Check off all completed subtasks
#    - Remove any "Next Steps" instructions that are now complete
#
# 2. UPDATE CHANGELOG.md:
#    - Add a new entry under the appropriate section (Added, Changed, Fixed, etc.)
#    - Include a brief description and the git commit hash if available
#    - Ensure the version and date are correct
#
# 3. UPDATE .cline/memory.md:
#    - Update "📅 Last Updated" with current date
#    - Update "Session Focus" with what was worked on
#    - Update "🎯 Current Project Status" checkboxes
#    - Add new "Latest Session Notes" section with:
#      * Summary of what was accomplished
#      * Key decisions made
#      * Any new files/endpoints created
#      * What's ready for next phase
#    - Move previous session notes down (keep history)
#
# 4. SUGGEST GIT ACTIONS:
#    - Suggest appropriate commit message(s)
#    - Remind about branch merge if on feature branch
#
# 5. SUMMARIZE:
#    - Provide brief summary of completed work
#    - Note what's next in the backlog

# =============================================================================
# 🧠 SESSION MEMORY
# =============================================================================

# At the end of significant work sessions, update .cline/memory.md with:
# - Decisions made and their rationale
# - Current state of work in progress
# - Known issues or TODOs
# - Any context that would help future sessions

